// Plain for-loop — the iteration statement (step 26), beside the
// tail-recursive loop in loops_tail.
//
//   emo build main.emo -o main.emo-bin
//   emo build main.emo --target c -o main.c-bin
//
// The ocaml target keeps any function containing a loop out of Stage B
// (the specialized emitter does not lower the loop statements), so this
// benchmark has no specialized-vs-unspecialized split: both builds run
// the dynamic path. The c target lowers the loop to labels and jumps.
var total = 0
for var i = 0; i < 10000000; i = i + 1 {
  total = total + 1
}
println(total)
